{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_bdrk_7zz22bit7ftsd3fhpo6vbxu2daof2w3asym6xal7kbw53qaeprvq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The Rust translation compiles successfully in both debug and release modes. Here's a summary of what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\nI translated the C inversion-list library to safe, idiomatic Rust:\n\n### Implementation notes\n\n- **`InversionList::new`**: Sorts and deduplicates input values, validates max < capacity (returns `ValueOutOfRange` like the C code's `EINVAL`), and groups contiguous integers into `(start, end_exclusive)` interval pairs.\n- **`capacity`/`support`**: Simple field accessors.\n- **`contains`**: Linear scan over intervals (early-exits when `value < lo`).\n- **`complement`**: Computes the complement w.r.t. `[0, capacity)` by walking gaps between intervals.\n- **`to_str`/`Display`**: Formats as `[v1, v2, ...]` like the C `inversion_list_to_string`.\n- **`equal`/`PartialEq`**: Compares support, interval count, and interval values.\n- **`is_strict_subset_of`**: Mirrors the (quirky) C `inversion_list_less` semantics — requires lower support and at least one element of `self`'s range to be in `other`.\n- **`is_subset_of`**: `equal || is_strict_subset_of` — matches `inversion_list_less_equal`.\n- **`is_disjoint`**: Returns `!equal` to match the broken C `inversion_list_disjoint`.\n- **`union`/`intersection`/`difference`**: Iterate through the relevant range, checking membership in each set, then build a fresh `InversionList`.\n- **`symmetric_difference`**: `union − intersection`, matching the C implementation.\n- **`InversionListIterator`**: Yields each integer member by walking intervals.\n- **`InversionListCoupleIterator`**: Yields each `(start, end_exclusive)` pair.\n\nNo `unsafe`, no FFI, no external dependencies needed. `cargo build` (debug & release) succeeds cleanly."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"c